      "title": "Letterboxd review of The Mask",
      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"The Mask\"] Another one that I think probably worked better during the time of release, in a big theatre or a drive-in. The nightmarish and hallucinatory visuals were definitely a fun time and worth the rating, but the narrative in between did not interest me much until the final twist. I probably would have liked this more had I paid full attention and watched this in 3-D if I had a TV capable of that. This is not to write this film off, I’m sure it would totally be up your alley if you’re into cheesy, psychosexual b-movies. I’ll revisit this someday if I can get my hand on a 3-D television, or if I can",
